Removed the `keycloak`, `oidc`, `authomatic-github` and `authomatic-google` authentication providers from site creation: new sites use `pas.plugins.identity` through the `identity-keycloak`, `identity-oidc`, `identity-github` and `identity-google` providers, and creating a site with one of the old providers fails with `UnsupportedAuthenticationProvider`, naming its replacement. The shared schema definitions are now `identity-keycloak`, `identity-oidc`, `identity-github` and `identity-google`, so distributions have to update their `schema.json`. The `SITE_AUTHENTICATION_OIDC-*` and `SITE_AUTHENTICATION_AUTHOMATIC-*` environment variables are ignored with a warning, and the `setup_oidc_auth`, `setup_keycloak_auth` and `setup_authomatic` helpers are deprecated. Existing sites keep their `pas.plugins.oidc` and `pas.plugins.authomatic` configuration. @ericof
